From 77f9648cb7df2e708cd12db729bdea83e8fc326e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 11:25:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] player information: the table of the metadata levels in cells

The table of the levels on the Dolby Vision page (which the file has,
which Hades acts on, which the display is sent) was four strings in
columns of five characters, drawn in Mono26: its columns held only with
a monospaced font. Estuary's own fontset Arial has Mono26 in Arial, and
a skin with none of Estuary's fonts draws the dialog of system/hades in
its font13: there the plus and minus signs fall under other levels than
their own, and the table says what is not so.

The window system now also publishes each cell of the table
(hades.dv.lvfile.<level>, hades.dv.lvused.<level>,
hades.dv.lvsent.<level>: PLAYERINFO::LevelCells() of the rows of
LevelTable()), cleared with the rest where no table is published, and
the page draws each cell in a column of its own (HadesLevelCell, 78 px
apart: five characters of Mono26, as the strings were), the names of
the levels as the skin's text. With Estuary's fonts the table looks as
it did; with any other font its columns hold. system/hades is made again
by make-playerinfo.py.

Host test (outside the tree): test_info.cpp checks LevelCells() on the
rows of a table (it does not build against the header before); 3
mutants are killed. measure_all.py: 0 that do not fit with Estuary's
fonts, and none cut with every font a font13 of 36 px.
validate_skin.py and validate_hades_dialog.py pass.
WinSystemGbmGLESContext.cpp compiles with the commands of the last
build.
